We intermittently get null price rules, and once on an old JDK a thread spun at 100% CPU inside rule(). Identify all thread-safety problems in this class and give a correct version that never blocks readers during a reload.
PricingRegistry.java:
public class PricingRegistry {
    private static PricingRegistry instance;
    private final Map<String, PriceRule> rules = new HashMap<>();
    private long loadedAt;

    public static PricingRegistry get() {
        if (instance == null) {
            synchronized (PricingRegistry.class) {
                if (instance == null) {
                    instance = new PricingRegistry();
                    instance.reload();
                }
            }
        }
        return instance;
    }

    public PriceRule rule(String sku) {
        if (System.currentTimeMillis() - loadedAt > 60_000) {
            reload();
        }
        return rules.get(sku);
    }

    private void reload() {
        rules.clear();
        for (PriceRule r : RuleDao.loadAll()) {
            rules.put(r.sku(), r);
        }
        loadedAt = System.currentTimeMillis();
    }
}

